Some feature sets are too small or too specialized to take part in budget allocation, such as MACCS fingerprints (167 features) or log-likelihood ratios (3 features). Others, such as mutation features that record differences from a parent antibody, carry meaning only beside a full representation. They cannot contribute many features, so including them would distort the budget split. We therefore add them as augmentation, calling the finished hybrid $\mathbf{H}$ the base and the feature sets that supply extra features the donors.

