Blocks of the top $k \in \{0, 5, 10, 20, 40\}$ ranked features, capped at the number of candidates, are each added to the base. Each is scored with the downstream model on the internal-validation samples. The chosen $k^*$ has the best score and must beat $k=0$, which wins ties, so keeping no extras is the default. Five block choices instead of about 50 accept-or-reject decisions leave less room to overfit a small validation set \citep{Cawley2010}. The chosen donors and feature positions are stored and re-extracted for the outer fold.

