The hybrid is compared with the best single base representation at its full number of features, which is what a user would otherwise run. This comparator is chosen per downstream model and per fold from the search's scores on the outer training samples. It is then refit on those samples and scored on the same held-out samples as the hybrid, so it can differ between folds. The hybrid is held to its budget, so the comparator is often many times wider. Both widths are recorded for every fold, since a difference between the two scores is partly a difference in width. The main quantity per fold is the hybrid's score minus that of the best single representation, signed so that a positive value means the hybrid scored better (for RMSE the sign is flipped).
