Each comparison is reported as its per-fold differences and their spread across the 5 folds. We use no significance tests and no confidence intervals, because 5 fold scores are correlated through shared training molecules. No unbiased estimator of the variance of $k$-fold cross-validation exists, and estimates that ignore the overlap underestimate it \citep{Bengio2004}.

