Two further studies come from a collaboration with the Oxford Protein Informatics Group. The first repeats the activity-cliff QSAR setting of \citet{Dablander2023} on three targets, with five scaffold folds. Dopamine D2 (6,333 compounds) and factor Xa (3,605) come from ChEMBL, and the SARS-CoV-2 main protease (1,924) comes from the COVID Moonshot project. Each target's pool should hold 10 representations, but GROVER and SMI-TED were not built, so the search draws on eight. The downstream models are LightGBM and the DNN, and the metric is the mean absolute error (MAE) in log units of activity.

