All four separate-site experiments run on Caco-2 and LogD, with five folds grouped by scaffold family and three seeds, the DNN and SVM, and budgets of 500 to 2{,}000 features. In the main one, each site holds the same molecules but one family of representations: substructure fingerprints, physicochemical descriptors or pretrained embeddings. It compares the best single family, picked on the training molecules, with one feature selection over all families. It also compares both with one selection per family at an even share of the budget. When a family is narrower than its share, the rest goes to the other families, so the even split can build fewer features than one selection over all families. The built widths are recorded on every fold.

