LogD can be read chemically (Figure~\ref{fig:blueprint_logd}). The SVM's hybrid picked 372 features on all five folds. Of these, 38 are Mordred descriptors and 36 are ECFP4 bits. The rest come from eight representations whose features carry no names. Among the descriptors are Crippen's calculated logP (SLogP), the number of basic groups (nBase) and several surface areas binned by partial charge (PEOE\_VSA). There are also counts of secondary amine and aromatic nitrogen environments. Among the bits are tertiary amine environments, in which a nitrogen is bonded to three carbons (\texttt{CN(C)C}), and aryl chloride environments. Unlike logP, which counts only the neutral form of a molecule, logD at pH 7.4 counts every charge state. At that pH a basic amine is largely protonated, which lowers logD below logP. A model of LogD should therefore need both lipophilicity and basicity. The hybrid picked both, on every fold, from two different representations.

