The hybrid needs data. Its gains are consistent on datasets of a few thousand samples and inconsistent on datasets of a few hundred. On those smaller datasets the search's internal scores overstate what the chosen hybrid delivers by up to 0.16 Spearman (Section~\ref{sec:method:results_overfit}), and its prediction intervals cover too few held-out samples. Most of the antibody datasets in this chapter are of that size. The antibody results therefore say as much about dataset size as about antibodies, and these datasets cannot separate the two. Whether the best hybrid settings follow measurable properties of a dataset is the question of the experiment still to be reported in Section~\ref{sec:method:results_single}.

