The hybrid can only select from what the pool offers. The antibody pools are mostly protein and antibody language models of the same sequence, several of them variants of ESM-2. The antibody hybrids therefore had few representations of different kinds to combine. Frozen embeddings also set a ceiling: no signal can be added beyond what the inputs contain. Integrating many foundation models, each with its own dependencies and hardware, is difficult engineering, and the burden grows with the number of models.

