\subsubsection{Selected by a detector}
% TODO: manual review
The main cleanup experiment takes the out-of-fold forest residual as its detector and crosses it with each action above. It also grades the cliff-aware gap as a detector beside it. A second experiment asks whether to delete a flagged molecule or keep it, and keeps it either with a lower weight or with a moved label. Its control deletes the same number of molecules at random, at five seeds. A third experiment replaces the forest residual with each of five detectors in turn: the cliff-aware gap, and the GP, the heteroscedastic GP, the variance-head network and NGBoost. Each deletes its top 5\%, 10\% or 20\%. Where the detector has its own prediction, it also moves every label toward that prediction. The share moved is given by Equation~\ref{eq:noise:move}, or by $c_i = \alpha s_i/(1 + \alpha s_i)$, which uses the score in its own units.
