On the first outer fold, noisy labels in QSAR data could be found, and in several settings corrected. Corrections worked best with a flag. Raising labels clipped at an assay limit won back half to three quarters of the lost RMSE on the small-molecule datasets, with no detector. With a detector, deleting or relabeling flagged molecules helped under label flips and outliers. It passed random and shuffled controls on hERG, hERG $K_i$, Buchwald--Hartwig and three antibody datasets. On clean QM9 labels deletion never helped, so the deletion gains are noise removed. The hybrid stays ahead of the single representation on small molecules through every treatment, and the ranking of noise-handling methods depends on the feature space they run in.

